    "explanation": "Both sides' arithmetic is correct and the tribunal adopts it. The governing distance is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00104, 34.17 km), not the rounded trip-record copy of 34.2 km (POL-RD-01). Against the booked optimal of 27.1 km the excess is 7.07 km, or 26.09%, so a route deviation is established and the rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged. The driver, however, points to a specific artifact and clause: the LTA DataMall advisory ADV-20260716-007 (EV-ADVIS-00104-01, weight 1.0), a HIGH-severity accident blocking 2 of 3 lanes on the PIE towards Tuas after Eunos Link, active 20:02-21:35 on the very corridor the optimal route uses, with the trace leaving the PIE before the blocked segment and rejoining on the AYE. POL-RD-03 therefore exonerates, but only up to its cap: min(7.07, 1.30 x (30.1 - 27.1) + 1.00) = 4.90 km. The closure-adjusted optimal is 27.1 + 4.90 = 32.0 km, with duration scaled to 34.0 x (32.0/27.1) = 40.1 minutes (amended_optimal_duration_min is null, so the scaled figure governs). The fare is METERED with surge 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, so POL-RD-02 runs and POL-RD-11 does not: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 32.0 + 0.28 x 40.1) x 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee = 39.828; charged_total is 43.41; refund = 43.41 - 39.828 = 3.582, rounded UP to SGD 3.60. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and below 90% of the charge, so the rider receives SGD 3.60, not the SGD 14.00 claimed. No ERP, toll, surcharge or waiting fee appears on the breakdown, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and no billing-integrity correction arises. The driver's 20:38 chat message ('accident on PIE after eunos, i go ECP instead ok') and the rider's reply are consistent with the LTA advisory; POL-RD-04 does not apply because the diversion was proposed by the driver rather than requested by the rider, and chat_message.waypoint_hint is null, so the rider-instruction exoneration cannot run. The second advisory (EV-ADVIS-00104-02) is impaired at weight 0.25 (issue codes ADVISORY_UNCORROBORATED and UNVERIFIED_SOURCE), describes a CTE corridor this trip never enters, is relied on by neither party, and so carries no fact and does not cap confidence. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: identifiers match across all three core artifacts, the trace is unimpaired (283 fixes at a 10-second interval, no gaps), no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing or out-of-window artifact, and the refund is far below SGD 150. Because the deviation is not material (26.09% is under 50% and 7.07 km is under 8.0 km) and the driver's trailing-90-day counters are well under threshold, POL-RD-06 gives no uplift and no conduct referral. The driver is not owed compensation: the billed 34.2 km already exceeds the traced 34.17 km, so there is no unbilled shortfall under POL-RD-04."
